    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d512">

                <pb facs="0649" n="335" xml:id="pg335"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 300.115/1058</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Page</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                        when="1914-11-02">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">November 2, 1914</hi>.</date>
                    <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 11:45 p.m.</hi>] </dateline>
                <p rendition="#center">[Telegram]</p>
                <p>964. Your 433, October 31. Sir Edward Grey promises to give me such a report as
                    you ask on the ship <hi rendition="#italic">Kroonland</hi> at earliest moment
                    possible. Its detention is not a seizure.</p>
                <p> Sir Edward informs me that his Government found evidence that the copper on the
                    Italian steamers <hi rendition="#italic">San Giovanni</hi> and <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Regina d’Italia</hi> was destined for belligerent
                    territory. This Government therefore prohibits its delivery and will itself buy
                    it and pay for it. The delay of the steamers was caused by the fact that the
                    Copper was at the bottom of the ships. They have been allowed to proceed under
                    guarantee that the copper will be delivered to British authorities on return
                    voyage.</p>
                <closer>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Ambassador</hi>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
